From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:35:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: always set explicit_pad_B when laying out an image

000362f6ff4 ("panvk: reserve the overfetch slack for explicit 24/96-bit
image layouts") set panvk_image_plane::explicit_pad_B only for explicit
24/96-bit planes. vkGetDeviceImageMemoryRequirements() and the sparse
memory requirement queries initialize a panvk_image on the stack, so for
every other image the field kept stack garbage and the reported size
differed from vkGetImageMemoryRequirements() on a created image:
dEQP-VK.memory.requirements.create_info.image.{regular,transient}_tiling_*
and dEQP-VK.api.invariance.memory{,_dedicated}_requirements_matching
failed.

Assign the field for every plane in panvk_image_init_layouts().

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_image.c | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_image.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_image.c
index 45b8ccd0da2..a3950615716 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_image.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_image.c
@@ -499,10 +499,13 @@ panvk_image_init_layouts(struct panvk_image *image,
 
       /* Explicit layouts are exact. Reserve the same overfetch slack in the
        * memory requirements as a layout we choose has, so an imported image
-       * needs as much memory as the exported one it describes. */
-      if (explicit_info &&
-          pan_image_needs_overfetch_pad(pan_img->props.format, pan_plane))
-         image->planes[plane].explicit_pad_B = PAN_IMAGE_OVERFETCH_PAD_B;
+       * needs as much memory as the exported one it describes. Always set
+       * it: vkGetDeviceImageMemoryRequirements() and the sparse queries
+       * initialize a panvk_image on the stack. */
+      image->planes[plane].explicit_pad_B =
+         explicit_info &&
+         pan_image_needs_overfetch_pad(pan_img->props.format, pan_plane) ?
+         PAN_IMAGE_OVERFETCH_PAD_B : 0;
 
       if (!is_disjoint(image) && !explicit_info)
          plane_layout.offset_B += image->planes[plane].plane.layout.data_size_B;
